Subject: [PATCH] feat(acceptance): single PC gate over every T-01..T-18
 criterion
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

20 tasks map to one command, evidence files, status, and — when blocked —
a reason plus a concrete handoff artifact, so "done" stops meaning "a
human believes it". verify_pc_acceptance.py always validates structure
(exit 2 on a bad manifest, blocked entries must carry reason+handoff),
runs each completed command with --run, and exits 3 under
--allow-blocked while blocked work remains.

Also records this sweep's outcomes: T-11 closed on a real Electron NetLog
plus the Google Fonts egress fix, T-12 closed on two overwrite installs
that left seeded memories/notes/sessions byte-identical, and the T-16
failure ledger (58 of 65 fixed, 7 residual Windows/environment items).
